Title: Extension Service Workers
Shortname: webextensions-service-workers
Level: 1
Group: webextensions
Status: w3c/ED
URL: https://w3c.github.io/webextensions/specification/extension-service-workers.html
Editor: Patrick Kettner, Google, patrickkettner@google.com
Abstract: A WebExtension can declare a service worker as its <a href="https://w3c.github.io/webextensions/specification/#key-background">background</a> context. Because WebExtensions have a permission model and user expectations that differ from those of web content, that service worker has access to capabilities that other service workers do not. This specification defines [=extension service workers=], what distinguishes their realms for WebIDL, and what a specification that exposes a capability only to them has to define.
